                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                            <span>Is the lactate test painful or invasive?</span>
                            <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
                        </button>
                        <div class="faq-answer">
                            <p><strong>Not at all!</strong> The test involves small finger pricks (similar to blood glucose testing) to collect tiny blood samples. Most athletes feel:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Slight pinch sensation during prick (less than a mosquito bite)</li>
                                <li>No lingering pain or discomfort</li>
                                <li>No downtime - you can train normally afterward</li>
                                <li>Safe and used by everyone from recreational to Olympic athletes</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p>The test itself is a progressive workout, so you'll be focused on the exercise, not the finger pricks!</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
                            <span>How accurate are consumer wearables compared to lab testing?</span>
                            <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i>
                        </button>
                        <div class="faq-answer">
                            <div class="wearable-comparison">
                                <h4>Consumer Wearable vs. Lab Testing Accuracy:</h4>
                                <table class="comparison-table">
                                    <thead>
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Metric</th>
                                            <th>Consumer Watch</th>
                                            <th>Lab Testing</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Heart Rate</td>
                                            <td>±5-10 bpm</td>
                                            <td>±1 bpm (ECG chest strap)</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>VO2max Estimate</td>
                                            <td>±10-15% error</td>
                                            <td>Gold standard</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Lactate Threshold</td>
                                            <td>❌ Cannot measure</td>
                                            <td>Direct measurement</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>LT1 & LT2 Zones</td>
                                            <td>❌ Cannot determine</td>
                                            <td>Accurate inflection points</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Sweat Sodium</td>
                                            <td>❌ Cannot measure</td>
                                            <td>Lab analysis</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Training Zones</td>
                                            <td>Formula estimates</td>
                                            <td>Individualized from data</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                                <p class="comparison-note"><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Wearables are great for tracking trends, but only direct lactate testing gives you accurate, personalized zones. We recommend using both - lab testing for zone calibration, wearables for daily monitoring.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
